    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup is anchored today by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.27), our two most potent offensive threats. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a high-efficiency matchup against Warren, bolstered by a +16% park factor and dynamic platoon advantages. Simultaneously, **Jackson Merrill** draws a favorable pairing against Stock; while he faces a slight park penalty, the combination of SP skill, platoon alignment, and beneficial wind patterns makes him an elite start. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66), **Kyle Tucker** (74.09), and **Andy Pages** (71.03) also clear the 70-point threshold, rounding out a top-heavy order designed to capitalize on favorable park conditions and weak SP profiles to secure necessary counting stats in Roto.\n\nWe have a cluster of mid-tier options, with **Sam Antonacci** (61.82) and **Jacob Wilson** (61.68) earning starts based on favorable lineup positioning and order-driven plate appearance projections. The most difficult decision this morning involved **Dominic Smith** (51.37), who was the first player left on the bench. Despite a solid platoon edge, his raw efficiency score simply could not surpass the incumbents in our outfield and utility slots; the optimizer prioritized the higher ceiling of **Jacob Wilson** against Lugo. Note that **Nasim Nunez** carries some risk, as his score of 53.75 is contingent on the assumption he bats 8th; should that move down, his efficiency will crater further. With **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Luis Robert Jr.** officially sidelined, we are relying on our depth to maintain our competitiveness in SB and AVG, keeping a close eye on the late-breaking lineups for **Nasim Nunez**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Coby Mayo** to ensure our projections hold.",
